  {
   "id": 25,
   "type": "Note",
   "pos": [
    2380,
    780
   ],
   "size": [
    420,
    380
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 6,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "title": "How this works",
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "Note"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "MASKED CHARACTER REPLACEMENT\n\nThe mask does the replacing, not the prompt \u2014 so this does not depend on\n[video editing] existing in the open weights.\n\nSIZES MUST MATCH. The H3 node's width/height/length have to equal the\nsource clip's, or the encoded source will not line up with the latent and\nthe node will say so.\n\nMASK TOO TIGHT IS THE COMMON FAILURE. Each latent cell covers 16 px and\n~3.4 frames, so the mask is unioned over time and dilated. If you see\nslivers of the ORIGINAL person at the edges of fast motion, raise dilate.\n\nfeather softens the boundary so the model blends instead of butting up\nagainst a wall. Spatial edges behave far better than temporal ones.\n\ninvert = keep the person, replace the room instead.\n\nSAM2 CANNOT READ TEXT. Florence2 does the reading: type the thing\nto replace into Florence2Run.text_input, it returns a box, and SAM2\ntracks that box through the clip. Change the phrase, not the graph."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
